<Layout title="Blog - Swastik Industries" current="blog">
<main><div class="page-hero"><img class="bg" src="/assets/f57.jpg" alt=""><div class="wrap"><div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Blog</div><h1>Blog</h1><p>Short notes on choosing and specifying cable management, earthing and structures.</p></div></div><section><div class="wrap"><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="tx" style="padding:1.6rem"><h3>Perforated or ladder cable tray: which to choose</h3><p>Perforated trays give ventilation and make cable tie-down easy. Ladder trays are used where cable loads are heavier or spans are longer.</p><p>Both are made from 1.6 mm to 3.0 mm sheet in standard lengths of 2.5 m or 3.0 m. Send the cable load, span and site conditions and we will confirm the section.</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="tx" style="padding:1.6rem"><h3>Pre-galvanised or hot dip galvanised finish</h3><p>Pre-galvanised sheet is suited to indoor and dry locations. Hot dip galvanising gives a heavier zinc coating for outdoor and corrosive environments.</p><p>Powder coated and painted finishes are also available where colour or appearance matters. Our hot dip galvanising is done in-house.</p></div></article><article class="card"><div class="tx" style="padding:1.6rem"><h3>Earthing material and the Indian standards</h3><p>GI plate, wire and strip are supplied to IS 4759, the specification for hot dip zinc coatings. GI earth electrodes follow IS 3043, the code of practice for earthing, and GI pipe follows IS 1239.</p><p>Copper earthing is available where the design calls for it.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="cta-band"><div class="wrap"><h2>Send your drawing or bill of quantities</h2><a class="btn" href="/contact">Request a quote</a></div></section></main>
</Layout>
